WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.018
Week 30: Por, Para, Passive, and Impersonal Se. explain purpose and cause describe processes report institutional action

2
00:00:09.018 --> 00:00:23.308
Form and meaning. Applying the form. Por expresses cause, means, or duration; para expresses purpose or destination; the passive voice uses ser + past participle, often with por + agent.

3
00:00:23.308 --> 00:00:48.798
Model set. El informe fue escrito por ella. Trabajo para mejorar el servicio. La ley fue aprobada por el congreso. Los datos fueron publicados ayer. Uso 'para' para expresar propósito. The report was written by her. I work to improve the service. The law was approved by congress. The data were published yesterday. I use 'para' to express purpose.

4
00:00:48.798 --> 00:00:59.077
Contrastive practice. Change the person, time, number, or level of formality in each model. Preserve the communicative purpose while the grammar changes.

5
00:00:59.077 --> 00:01:12.429
Production check. Say one original sentence for each function: explain purpose and cause; describe processes; report institutional action. Then write it and compare the spoken and written forms.

6
00:01:12.429 --> 00:01:38.559
Model language. El informe fue escrito por ella. — The report was written by her. Trabajo para mejorar el servicio. — I work to improve the service. La ley fue aprobada por el congreso. — The law was approved by congress. Los datos fueron publicados ayer. — The data were published yesterday. Uso 'para' para expresar propósito. — I use 'para' to express purpose.

7
00:01:38.559 --> 00:01:48.563
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
